1
00:00:01,722 --> 00:00:10,491
KYC & Compliance
Risk-based client due diligence and the compliance registers — from a new client to an approved KYC.

2
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:16,000
Sign in as Priya Ramdin — Relationship Manager
The relationship manager onboards the client

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:28,760
Clients ▸ Parties ▸ New: the client's identity and contact details
Tick PEP when the client holds a prominent public function

4
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:32,840
KYC & Compliance ▸ KYC Cases ▸ New
A case from a converted enquiry is opened for you automatically — here we open one by hand

5
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:35,160
Answer the risk questions
Product, onboarding channel, occupation, ownership structure and expected activity

6
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:41,840
Add the tax status for FATCA and CRS reporting
Group-level scope: one approved KYC can be relied on by every Genesis entity

7
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:46,160
The risk score is calculated for you
Country + PEP + product + channel + occupation + ownership + activity — weights from the risk-factor master

8
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:49,640
A PEP is always high risk: enhanced due diligence is now required
High-risk cases are approved by the MLRO and reviewed every year

9
00:00:49,640 --> 00:01:06,600
Docs tab: the Individual KYC pack lists what is still missing
Upload what the client gave you — or email the client a secure upload link

10
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:09,640
All three items are in — the checklist shows nothing outstanding
Identity and address documents are reviewed and kept seven years (AML)

11
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:13,960
Edit the case and tick “Document checklist complete”
Under verification will not accept the case without it

12
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:26,440
Move the case along the KYC pipeline
Initiated ▸ Documents pending ▸ Under verification ▸ Screening

13
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:32,120
Entering Screening checks the client against sanctions, PEP and adverse-media lists
The provider answers in seconds and the result is written on the case

14
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:36,800
Screening result: potential match — with the provider reference and date
The PEP hit is logged for Compliance to triage and Compliance is alerted

15
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:40,400
The hit itself sits behind the compliance barrier
The RM only sees that one is open — Compliance triages it

16
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:48,040
Screening done: move the case to Risk assessed
This stage needs a screening result and date — the automation already filled them

17
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:51,720
Now try Pending approval…
For a high-risk client the CRM checks the enhanced due diligence first

18
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:55,200
Blocked: high risk needs verified source of wealth and EDD notes
The message tells the RM exactly what is missing

19
00:01:55,240 --> 00:02:05,120
Record the enhanced due diligence on the case
Source of funds verified + EDD notes (source of wealth, senior management approval)

20
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:09,880
Move to Pending approval again
This time the gate lets it through

21
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:12,840
An approval request is raised automatically
Standard or medium risk → Compliance Officer · High risk or PEP → MLRO

22
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:21,560
Staff declare gifts and hospitality in the Gifts & Hospitality Register
Anything above MUR 5,000 needs a compliance decision

23
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:24,320
8,500 is above the threshold, so the declaration goes to Compliance for approval

24
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,520
Compliance reviews the screening hit
True match · False positive · Escalated to MLRO — with a rationale

25
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:31,200
Sign in as Fatima Hossenbux — Compliance Officer
Compliance officer: screening triage, registers, approvals

26
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:36,920
Set the disposition and record why
A domestic PEP is not a sanctions match — escalate it to the MLRO for sign-off

27
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:39,480
An escalation alerts the MLRO
A true match would also stop the case reaching approval

28
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:47,240
Tools ▸ Approvals: the gift declaration is waiting for Compliance
Standard-risk KYC sign-offs arrive here too

29
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:54,880
Add an issuer to the restricted list
For example while Genesis advises on a deal and holds inside information

30
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:58,360
Traders and portfolio managers are alerted at once
Personal-dealing requests in this issuer are refused automatically · watch-list entries stay with Compliance

31
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:09,360
A client asks for a copy of their personal data (DPA 2017)
Data Subject Requests: Received ▸ Verifying identity ▸ In progress ▸ Completed — 30 days to respond

32
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:13,920
Acknowledged and assigned to Compliance; respond-by date = received + 30 days
First step: verify the requester's identity

33
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:32,680
Verify identity, prepare the response, record the completion date
In progress needs identity verified · Completed needs the response and date

34
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:34,120
Suspicious transaction reports sit behind the MLRO barrier
Anyone may raise one — only the MLRO sees them (no tipping-off)

35
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:38,080
Even the compliance officer sees no reports here
The records are concealed: not listed, not searchable, not counted

36
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:39,040
High-risk and PEP cases are signed off by the MLRO
Tools ▸ Approvals

37
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:43,320
Sign in as Olivier Maurel — MLRO
Money Laundering Reporting Officer

38
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:51,520
The request shows the risk score and the EDD notes
Open the case from the link if more detail is needed — then approve or reject

39
00:03:51,520 --> 00:04:03,200
The case moves to Approved by itself
Outcome, decision date and next review (1 year for high risk) are recorded

40
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:09,440
On the client record, KYC status is now approved
Loans can be disbursed, accounts funded and relationships activated

41
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:16,800
The MLRO sees the STR register
Raised ▸ MLRO review ▸ Filed with FIU (needs the FIU reference and date) / Closed — no filing

42
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:20,833
Who may see which zone is managed in Tools ▸ Access & Barriers
Covered in its own tutorial

43
00:04:20,833 --> 00:04:28,520
KYC & Compliance
The CRM screens, scores and routes — staff answer the questions and make the decisions.
